173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (The E-Commerce Product Entity-Resolution and Matching Platform is a system designed to identify and match similar products listed across different online stores. E-commerce websites often use different product names, descriptions, brands, and formats for the same product, making it difficult to compare them accurately. This project solves this problem by using Data Structures and Algorithms to detect products that represent the same real-world item.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (The system processes product information using techniques such as tokenization, inverted indexing, Jaccard similarity, and Levenshtein distance to measure the similarity between product listings. A weighted matching score is then calculated to determine whether two products are likely to be the same. Union-Find is used to group matching products into clusters, while a canonical product is selected to represent each group. The platform can also help users compare prices across different sellers, making product searching faster, more accurate, and more convenient.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
